   "spoken": "The key subtlety — Bb7 rather than Ba6. The point is that after f5 and the exchanges, you justify the bishop by striking the centre with d5; on a6 that same break doesn't work. That's the method of comparison — the way to understand why the engine prefers one square over another.",
